{
  "dom_id": "step-q74385",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x-2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242844/assets/345fdaf3f301848b35448b710f240a308cfaadc1bae2729a5b0ddfa76793f6cb.png)\n\nSince we have $y=\\frac{1}{x-2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ to the *right* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated to the right by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x=0$ is also translated to the right by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242844/assets/8e73ed9744751224b9ef0bba78812f3681a9a98275f172b90552abcd1c6fc7d8.png)",
